AMBASSADOR DAMBAZAU HOSTS PLATEAU STATE GOVERNOR IN BEIJING, CHAMPIONS STRATEGIC PARTNERSHIPS FOR DEVELOPMENT 🇳🇬🇨🇳

His Excellency Barr. Caleb Manasseh Mutfwang, Executive Governor of Plateau State, paid a courtesy call on the Embassy of the Federal Republic of Nigeria in Beijing during his visit to China to explore partnership opportunities with potential Chinese investors.

The visit reflects the growing recognition among Nigeria’s subnational governments of the importance of international engagement in attracting investment, accessing technology, strengthening economic cooperation and unlocking new pathways for sustainable development.

His Excellency Lt Gen Ambassador Abdulrahman Bello Dambazau, CFR, PhD, reaffirmed the Embassy’s readiness to support and facilitate constructive engagements between Nigerian states and credible Chinese investors, with the ultimate objective of advancing Nigeria’s broader developmental aspirations.

The initiative aligns with the Comprehensive Strategic Partnership established in 2024 by President Bola Ahmed Tinubu of Nigeria and President Xi Jinping of China, providing a framework for deeper cooperation across key sectors of national development.

From infrastructure and industrialisation to agriculture, energy, technology, education and healthcare, the partnership presents opportunities for Nigerian states to identify relevant areas of cooperation and translate international relationships into practical development outcomes for their people.

The Embassy remains committed to serving as a bridge between Nigeria’s development priorities and the opportunities available in China, supporting initiatives that promote investment, technology transfer, local capacity development, job creation and inclusive economic growth.

When states connect with global opportunities, diplomacy becomes a practical instrument of development.

